      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting alloy can be produced by conventional powder metallurgy or similar techniques.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is addition of 0.5–1 wt% Hf during alloy synthesis.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf will preferentially segregate to grain boundaries and interfaces in W38Ta36Cr15V11.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf segregation will produce stable Hf-rich interfacial zones.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf-rich grain boundaries will have enhanced sink efficiency for irradiation-induced point defects and small defect clusters.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Trapping irradiation defects at Hf-decorated interfaces will disrupt diffusion pathways needed for precipitate nucleation and growth.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf doping will suppress radiation-induced precipitation under energetic-particle irradiation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At approximately 8 dpa and 600–800°C, the Hf-doped alloy will have approximately 30–50% less precipitation than the undoped alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-doped alloy will have a lower density of irradiation-induced defect clusters than the undoped alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-doped alloy will retain negligible irradiation hardening, with hardness changes within approximately 10% of the baseline response.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Undoped nanocrystalline W38Ta36Cr15V11 exhibits measurable radiation-induced precipitation at approximately 8 dpa and 600–800°C.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Undoped nanocrystalline W38Ta36Cr15V11 exhibits minimal irradiation hardening under those conditions.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The claimed effect applies up to approximately 8 dpa within 600–800°C when the Hf concentration is 0.5–1 wt%.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Temperatures outside 600–800°C, doses beyond approximately 8 dpa, or Hf contents outside 0.5–1 wt% may produce different outcomes.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf addition will make the nanocrystalline alloy more amenable to practical bulk fabrication.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
